# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.dSYM/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json

# Test server binary and temp files
test/integration/testserver/testserver
test/integration/.test-server-url

# Compiled example binaries (each example dir builds a binary named after itself)
examples/generate-text/generate-text
examples/streaming-cli/streaming-cli
examples/tools-agent/tools-agent
examples/structured-output/structured-output
examples/chat-server/chat-server

# Node dependencies (integration/conformance test harnesses, tooling)
node_modules/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
